{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they did not listen to Moses.</b> Not because they did not trust in YHWH and in Moses His servant, but rather from shortness of spirit and from harsh labor — like a person who longs to die because of the suffering he is in and rejects his life." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״מקוצר רוח״ — 'from shortness of spirit' — hinted to them the end of the redemption, which is a short reckoning, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 12): ״ויהי מקץ שלשים שנה וארבע מאות שנה ויהי בעצם היום הזה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "The cited verse 'ויהי מקץ שלשים שנה וארבע מאות שנה' does not correspond to the Masoretic text of Exodus 12:41 ('והיה מקץ שלשים שנה וארבע מאות שנה'); translated hyper-literally as printed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:25.975690433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}